  "description": "Reid Quest 2 ST eBike | Electric step-through bike\nPowerful, comfortable and built to go further – an electric step-through bike designed for confident commuting, leisure rides and exploring light trails.\nThe Reid Quest 2 ST eBike combines a powerful mid-drive motor with a practical step-through frame and quality components, making it a capable choice for everyday journeys, longer rides and exploring varied terrain.\nIts advanced alloy step-through frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 36V 417Wh battery, creating a clean, streamlined design with a convenient low-step frame for easier mounting and dismounting. At its heart, an Ananda 250W mid-motor delivers smooth, natural-feeling electric assistance to support everyday riding and help tackle hills and longer distances. An Ananda D18 Bluetooth display provides clear ride information and app compatibility.\nThe Uding D5 suspension fork offers 100mm of travel with a lockout function, helping absorb bumps and vibrations across uneven surfaces while allowing riders to lock the suspension when a firmer setup is preferred.\nA Shimano 9-speed drivetrain offers a wide gear range, combining a Cues shifter and rear derailleur with an 11-46T Shimano cassette to make tackling varied gradients easier. Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors provide dependable stopping power and controlled braking.\nKenda 27.5 x 2.35-inch tyres deliver grip, stability and comfort across urban roads, cycle paths and light trails. Completing the setup are 640mm alloy riser handlebars, an adjustable 85mm stem, a Comfort Plus saddle and ergonomic lock-on grips, creating a relaxed and supportive riding position.\nThe Quest 2 ST eBike is ideal for:\n\nEveryday commuters, with smooth electric assistance for regular journeys\n\nEasy mounting and dismounting, thanks to its practical step-through frame\n\nRiders tackling hills and longer distances, with a 250W Ananda mid-motor\n\nLonger leisure rides, supported by an integrated 417Wh battery and comfortable riding position\n\nLight trail exploration, with a 100mm Uding D5 suspension fork and grippy Kenda tyres\n\nRiders wanting versatile gearing, with a Shimano Cues 9-speed drivetrain and wide-range 11-46T cassette\n\nRiders who value controlled braking, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and 180mm rotors\n\nComfort-focused cyclists, with 640mm riser handlebars, an adjustable stem and ergonomic finishing touches\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
